libslic3r: skip GCode::append_full_config when no bundle loaded

Both GCode::_do_export branches (BBL and non-BBL) unconditionally call
append_full_config to dump every print config option as a `; key = value`
comment block at the head of the .gcode. On Android with no preset
bundle loaded, one of the enum config options has a null name table and
ConfigOptionEnumsGenericTempl<false>::serialize_single_value
null-derefs.

Comment out both call sites. The dump is informational — readers /
re-importers tolerate its absence (BambuStudio / OrcaSlicer parse it
back when re-importing a .gcode, but Phase 0 doesn't re-import).

Retire-if: Phase 1 loads a real preset bundle (the BBL G-code reimport
flow stops being a JNI smoke test concern), or upstream initializes
ConfigOptionEnumsGeneric name tables eagerly.

---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp b/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp
index fe10cbcd41..2fbad6ea1f 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp
@@ -2571,8 +2571,13 @@ void GCode::_do_export(Print& print, GCodeOutputStream &file, ThumbnailsGenerato
     {
         if (is_bbl_printers) {
             file.write("; CONFIG_BLOCK_START\n");
+            // OrcaXR: append_full_config crashes on Android when no preset
+            // bundle is loaded — some enum option's name table is null and
+            // serialize_single_value derefs it. Skip the config dump for
+            // now; it's just a comment block consumers don't strictly
+            // need. Re-enable when Phase 1 wires real preset bundles.
             std::string full_config;
-            append_full_config(print, full_config);
+            // append_full_config(print, full_config);
             if (!full_config.empty())
                 file.write(full_config);
 
@@ -3444,8 +3449,11 @@ void GCode::_do_export(Print& print, GCodeOutputStream &file, ThumbnailsGenerato
             .c_str());
       file.write("\n");
       file.write("; CONFIG_BLOCK_START\n");
+      // OrcaXR: see comment on the BBL branch above. Skip the
+      // append_full_config dump; it crashes without a loaded preset
+      // bundle.
       std::string full_config;
-      append_full_config(print, full_config);
+      // append_full_config(print, full_config);
       if (!full_config.empty())
         file.write(full_config);
 
